<!-- SOCIO-ECONOMIC IMPACT -->
<section id="socioeconomic-impact">
  <h2>💰 Socio-Economic Factors and Their Impact on Performance</h2>
  <p>This section examines the four principal socio-economic levers—<strong>family income, parent education, internet access, and private tuition</strong>—and quantifies their relationship with HSC outcomes using mean comparisons, effect sizes (Cohen’s <em>d</em>), and statistical significance testing.</p>

  <h3>Family Income</h3>
  <p>Monthly family income ranges from 10,016 to 59,767 BDT (mean 34,888 BDT). When split into quartiles, HSC performance shows <strong>no meaningful income gradient</strong>:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Income Quartile</th><th class="num">Range (BDT)</th><th class="num">Mean HSC GPA</th><th class="num">Std. Dev.</th><th class="num">N</th></tr></thead>
